<title>ITALY: Italy's Ciampi says plan outlines welfare reform.</title>
<headline>Italy's Ciampi says plan outlines welfare reform.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi said the three-year econmomic plan approved by the cabinet Friday contained an outline of how the government would approach welfare state reforms.</p>
<p>Ciampi, speaking at a news conference, also said Italy's economy was starting to pick up in a climate of price stability.</p>
<p>The Treasury Minister also said the forecast interest bill on Italy's public debt mountain was 175 trillion lire in 1998 compared with 202 trillion lire in 1996.</p>
<p>Rome newsroom +396-6782505</p>
